#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152046 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/id #uuid "dd9a05fb-f01c-5ec2-a984-9d73584065ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-9683" :question/problem "![](images/79/793fd170c89b87cc168ead4bb92613135d503143a8b7f8dc7b7c39a3d2d065fa.png)\n\nWhich of the lines $p,q,r,$ or $s$ is the trend line of the scatter plot above?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](images/e2/e2f6a85400c916f198f9dd9fd8b04318d1d4c956c850f5e1e81968993b5d3d53.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152047 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/id #uuid "245065cc-c95c-5f93-bf7d-bbb6412a27e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9694" :question/problem "![](images/db/dbc57d2facbcf4bcf3b7617480384ea411d26be05d3fbbcf5edc6a14bc5ae216.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $(x_1,y_1)=(-4,5)$ and $(x_2,y_2)=(5,-4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-5}{5-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{9} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-1$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny = - x + b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,-4)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x+b \\\\ -4 & =-5+b \\\\ 1 & =b \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny = - x + 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152048 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/id #uuid "1a299957-af22-544b-af37-695f45065a3e" :question/math-academy-id "e-9695" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad0deee6d845c0241108567ce6b0c744604f1f6f50d9af0405523cd9501a96a0.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/72/722b5393babd1405c0330e9b4ed08c5030ddf6c69bd8b9e3f6c6d138f02c098c.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $(x_1,y_1)\\approx(4,4)$ and $(x_2,y_2)\\approx(6,7).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-4}{6-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=1.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny = 1.5 x + b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(4,4)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =1.5x+b \\\\ 4 & =1.5(4)+b \\\\ 4 & =6+b \\\\ -2 & =b \\\\ b & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny = 1.5x - 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f94c162-194f-58e0-9400-43b23d6578c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266717} {:answer/id #uuid "4ecc640c-3a6a-5538-8651-4c32a8e7ff05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266847} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9f6187-880c-581b-b8ee-90182d24ba69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267400} {:answer/id #uuid "b4357c31-8826-5245-a3f9-4fb4a95a2778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267753} {:answer/id #uuid "cb37720d-692e-511f-88aa-12613046c07a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c9f6187-880c-581b-b8ee-90182d24ba69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267400} :answer-field/id #uuid "f77a459d-d81e-52ae-9d62-79923a033894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa90d9a6-e51c-5604-b79f-b37b09fca968" :question/math-academy-id "q-133633" :question/problem "![](images/c1/c1b4ec98039bb5c09f168afa77f8211585403b333ae70bce383dbf2101212848.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between age and years of work experience among a particular group of workers. Which of the following could be the trend line for this scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a straight line.\n\n![](images/c8/c8597282ec934e535a01fa6f22be95b958d0393a5d0c5cd6358a9a7e620ba6a5.png)\n\nWe see that the line $q$ best fits the given data set."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a8330d-2949-5275-8ef7-1d8c2aad018c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266457} {:answer/id #uuid "51c6897d-681a-5148-b0e4-5e4c742f09fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266875} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5dfb03-1e0c-5e04-bcb3-768a1f08285b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267111} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb9f832-afaa-53de-8b04-1f04f545d7d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267248} {:answer/id #uuid "b87b96e7-8f8b-57a8-af5b-d59e2f6da620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb9f832-afaa-53de-8b04-1f04f545d7d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267248} :answer-field/id #uuid "b94b8c75-abce-5204-b0c4-10e2b00ff092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3eefe541-d677-50bc-bb17-f1cdd88a5e62" :question/math-academy-id "q-133765" :question/problem "![](images/99/99cd0af2bcfd5148a49179203b6fff4831133d875fda9fa474d928eab5eb8f1c.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(4,1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,9).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cab51bf-eaf2-5abc-b4a1-4acce4c0e8e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266260} {:answer/id #uuid "444fe05d-ac45-5a39-b877-ad5c918a9509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-1.5x+8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266755} {:answer/id #uuid "465057ea-f72d-5922-8900-757d5103f708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0.5x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266772} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef3ceec-d83d-5f88-bf11-a49b1ced77a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-8.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267418} {:answer/id #uuid "996a9a45-c89a-558a-9360-bfaf4b103674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "996a9a45-c89a-558a-9360-bfaf4b103674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-0.5x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267529} :answer-field/id #uuid "087a018b-8368-5c1b-a439-96b28b3979ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be8af3f3-2d6e-5282-b124-c4fc21f05bfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-133769" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4b948bc417deab7c83cb40f53ad4b55fbfb169fc4ec761a9365856a9457a8f5.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/fd/fd3ce3de75fa9296c721e3f3a28bef241eae6350819c4cc7a54707921c0c1fe4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(2,7)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(8,4).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-7}{8-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{6} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=-0.5$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,7):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-0.5x+b \\\\ 7 & =-0.5(2)+b \\\\ 7 & =-1+b \\\\ 8 & =b \\\\ b & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-0.5x+8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "327d9a77-b2dd-57b1-b959-570684714bf9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Trendline of a Given Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19df2904-6b7c-58b7-88b2-f605d8ef8506" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266356} {:answer/id #uuid "206a46ed-1970-5316-95be-58e720077042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266429} {:answer/id #uuid "9f00bb6e-9294-56b5-992c-5b2f338a0360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267579} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4ceff1-9762-5e9a-86c1-ecb6e7702031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267682} {:answer/id #uuid "ada9a303-0bc7-52d4-9bc2-ee3bd198d19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ada9a303-0bc7-52d4-9bc2-ee3bd198d19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no linear trend in the data" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267713} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f754f6c-4370-57d3-9e5d-4f14615413c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "595cbfc4-8fff-5045-9e69-dae0c1acb047" :question/math-academy-id "q-134009" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f64050151e65151975954cdf169379c5ea6ee80b0348a6cb03706ab64c7c7105.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the trend line of the scatter plot?" :question/worked-solution "The plot shows that the data points are scattered along a curve, not a straight line.\n\n![](images/00/00fe583ae8b83bfef31c1914489be7794aa4b7b2850cd01243a46b8d86d1dddb.png)\n\nTherefore, there is no linear trend in the data."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e1f18b-1852-5af1-8499-7eb19e018ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266308} {:answer/id #uuid "184cd861-8c34-5268-9a33-ee4b1a82e271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266345} {:answer/id #uuid "1b7a5941-b902-5459-89a3-423d6555f39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266378} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4d098a-9ed0-542a-ad02-61052de5a409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266673} {:answer/id #uuid "f25133e5-029a-5434-834e-2ae8f93904ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12e1f18b-1852-5af1-8499-7eb19e018ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266308} :answer-field/id #uuid "06014dbd-b187-5859-8fef-b25bfa74ae6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268413}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2869212-3453-5179-ad24-03054774f50a" :question/math-academy-id "q-134011" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c55d326b26a8bb6831f38456b7b47878ef66a185090c7327cbb151c4e951be33.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63426ad7-4275-5ac3-854d-e91ec00dcbe3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3800c633-4663-5a7c-977b-4d0c6dda0f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266629} {:answer/id #uuid "53efa526-eb5e-5256-af09-1eec2833abff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{7}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266895} {:answer/id #uuid "aba8afc3-be94-5f08-8b22-73af4c6b41c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267693} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8916a0-dcf5-50b0-b591-84f24b525679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268274} {:answer/id #uuid "f31ff6ea-86e9-5bba-a3ed-309adf564a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aba8afc3-be94-5f08-8b22-73af4c6b41c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267693} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d24660-a466-52cd-ab29-3ad82a1272ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c42b7eb-86b2-59d5-8ce6-728291f9e718" :question/math-academy-id "q-134023" :question/problem "![](images/1c/1c9f30692222eaaed4cda6b608dcc1ccb01eefd6b5fa7730b5b8bb29c9f528b1.png)\n\nDetermine the equation of the trend line shown above." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(7,8).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{7-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=\\frac{6}{5}$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{6}{5}x+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{6}{5}(2)+b \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{12}{5}+b \\\\ 10 & =12+5b \\\\ -2 & =5b \\\\ b & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5}x-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f69d6d6-f65d-5ba2-a0d2-ec96450b904c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266563} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2b2005-e668-56d9-b3b4-b2d1d38ff629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266964} {:answer/id #uuid "99a06ebc-ac19-5f94-a156-eb204f48255f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267534} {:answer/id #uuid "a5340cd2-a9ed-55b6-9b11-313ff0af8372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267633} {:answer/id #uuid "e72106a0-7ad8-5146-bba3-a4016a76a043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f69d6d6-f65d-5ba2-a0d2-ec96450b904c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266563} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41ee374-e612-55c4-a15d-7afecd007c01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fec0ce3a-bf15-5c41-9f72-214fd8c31558" :question/math-academy-id "q-134025" :question/problem "![](images/c8/c8f6d0161777412704a9a80c0336af04a6968454d421913055024b6d0cf11c71.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/b5/b50fd1636cc2e1bb9d150eaba9cc25a3ccedff77e607bf22853004332a7c4ddc.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(3,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(5,3).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-6}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{2} \\\\  & =-1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268958 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "890526df-fd1a-5340-8732-efc0c1a1b0ae" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Equation of a Trendline"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099bdefa-f8d2-5acc-84b7-74bc261996fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266231} {:answer/id #uuid "2ee57d74-67d5-5b61-af35-96dd84de092c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266560} {:answer/id #uuid "33b80c4e-3ce7-5308-9505-f492c7dd9012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1.5x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266598} {:answer/id #uuid "90363514-ca92-5816-8b4b-8b82cf37e7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267426} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ad0a79-a3c4-5480-9db0-3f13ff4381f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2.5x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ee57d74-67d5-5b61-af35-96dd84de092c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266560} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d92bc77-95f8-5697-932c-a47df1e134b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "240005ae-034c-5e2f-9211-125231674030" :question/math-academy-id "q-134032" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d23d6a35343aebcb986118bd7c5bc720f00480706057ec900e55c75bac296ebb.png)\n\nEstimate the equation of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round both the slope and the $y$-intercept to the nearest $0.5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](images/66/663e4d77d51816641a9fa861f37893d9f986d5e2b00e605ed5eb4fc19d40eab4.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(5,5)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(7,9).$\n\nWe will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nFirst, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-5}{7-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $m=2$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=2x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to estimate the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can do this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(5,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x+b \\\\ 5 & =2(5)+b \\\\ 5 & =10+b \\\\ -5 & =b \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=2x-5.\n$$"}]}
